1
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:21,000
He led the last great outlaw raids !

2
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:36,000
The Cimarron Kid is a western film directed by Budd Boetticher.

3
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:51,000
Audie Murphy comes into his own as a Western star in this story.

4
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:06,000
Wrongly accused by crooked railroad officials of aiding a train heist by his old friends the
Daltons, he joins their gang and becomes an active participant in other robberies.

5
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:21,000
Betrayed by a fellow gang member, Murphy becomes a fugitive in the end.

6
00:31:30,000 --> 00:31:36,000
Seeking refuge at the ranch of a reformed gang member, he hopes to flee with the man's
daughter to South America, but he's captured in the end and led off to jail.

7
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:51,000
The girl promises to wait.

8
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
Bill Doolin / The Cimarron Kid, played by Audie Murphy.

9
00:47:15,000 --> 00:47:21,000
Carrie Roberts, played by Beverly Tyler.

10
00:52:30,000 --> 00:52:36,000
Bitter Creek Dalton, played by James Best.

11
00:57:45,000 --> 00:57:51,000
Cimarron Rose Adams (as Yvette Dugay), played by Yvette Duguay.

12
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
Dynamite Dick Dalton, played by John Hudson.

13
01:08:15,000 --> 01:08:21,000
Red Buck, played by Hugh O'Brian.

14
01:13:30,000 --> 01:13:36,000
The Cimarron Kid is a 1952 American western film directed by Budd Boetticher
and starring Audie Murphy, Beverly Tyler and Yvette Duguay.

15
01:18:45,000 --> 01:18:51,000
It was  produced and distributed by Universal Pictures.
